# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Before this, endings were inconsistent - most files CRLF, several MIXED within
# a single file. Any edit that rewrote a whole file normalised it as a side
# effect, so a 180-line change arrived as a 4,400-line diff and the real work was
# unreviewable. This file stops that recurring.
#
# LF rather than CRLF: the published packages ship this source to consumers on
# every platform, CI runs on Linux, and LF is what every tool here emits by
# default. Windows development is fully supported - modern editors and Git for
# Windows handle LF working trees without configuration.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Lockfiles are generated; keep them out of diffs and merges.
pnpm-lock.yaml -diff linguist-generated
deno.lock      -diff linguist-generated
